@@ -139,3 +139,44 @@ layers (`vxcheck`). What changed from the plan above, while building:
 
 Next: the hidden size (5120, from about 2,250 live dims at L8-L9) and with it the checkpoint
 (26.7 GB).
+
+## VFIR (custom-2, funct7 = 1, funct3 0; uop 81), 2026-11-04
+
+One complex Q15 sample through a transposed-form FIR of n <= 16 taps (`vx.py` has the exact
+contract). rs1 = x (xr | xi << 16), rs2 = dst 4, src 3 (v0..v7), h 3 (v8 + h), n 5, eoff 6, chain 1.
+Tap j (element pair eoff / 2 + j): y_j = z + rhu(h_j x / 2^15) per component, z = src's pair j - 1
+(j = 0: 0, or with chain the pair before the block in bank A seen as one 256-pair array, so
+64 taps chain over two registers). Record: VC slots 0, 1, 4, 5, 6, then yr, yi as words (4 tokens
+a tap), then rd = sat16(yr) | sat16(yi) << 16 of the last tap as a value record (NT for x0).
+Ping-pong src / dst between calls; the identity rd = sat16(sum_k rhu(g_k x[n - k] / 2^15)) with
+the taps stored reversed is checked against an independent oracle (`tests/test_rv_vfir_ref.py`).
+
+Circuit (no new heads, no new layer: 13 layers, 137 heads before and after):
+- slot 1 bit 11 (NEW) is 1 only here; the VEW MAC cases carry [1 - NEW].
+- bank A's VM query is an 8-bit (register, pair) form: the write's pair for every other op;
+  for NEW, (reg_a, hoff | j - 1) for j >= 1 and (reg_a, hoff) - 1 at j = 0 (L1 MLP nodes).
+- the RoPE multiply chain does the complex product: W1, W2 = the tap pair (bank B), F = (xr, -xi)
+  / (xi, xr) by parity from the config; z << 15 and 2^14 go into the same nibble columns, then
+  the shift by -15, so a word streams straight from the MAC.
+- the value record reads the last tap's words back through the lag head (VE lags 1-3, VH lags
+  1-3 added as columns of the existing head); core's v counter also restarts at VH (VX builds).
+
+## VPOW (custom-2, funct7 = 1, funct3 1; uop 82), 2026-11-04
+
+The power of n <= 32 complex int16 elements (`vx.py` has the exact contract). rs1 = src 3 (v0..v7,
+bank A only), n 6, eoff 6 (even, aligned to 2 n); rs2 unused. acc = sum (ar^2 + ai^2) mod 2^32 over
+the pairs (VM[src][eoff + 2 j], VM[src][eoff + 2 j + 1]). Record: VC slots 0, 1, 5, then per element
+the running sum as VE (bits 0-15) and VH (bits 16-31: bit 15 is data here), then rd = acc as a value
+record (NT for x0): 3 + 2 n + 1..3 tokens. Write target vsum, so the VM write and the vmx / vbest
+trackers stay off; vsum ends as acc's bits 0-30 sign-extended (VGET 1). Checked against an
+independent oracle in `tests/test_rv_vpow_ref.py`.
+
+Circuit (no new heads, no new layer):
+- NEW with write target vsum (wt bit 0) selects VPOW; the VFIR bank-A query terms carry [1 - wt0],
+  and VPOW adds (reg_a, hoff | vel): one pair an element.
+- the RoPE multiply chain: W1 = F1 = ar, W2 = F2 = ai (bank A's pair, F as nibbles of the read),
+  shift 0; the earlier running sum goes into the same nibble columns from the lags (VE lag 1 /
+  VH lag 0 at the VH, VE lag 2 / VH lag 1 at the VE; 0 at the first element), so both tokens of
+  an element stream straight from the MAC (bits 0-31 of its 40-bit sum).
+- the element count is VMAT's (slot 5 bits 1-7, its done node); the value record reads the last
+  sum back through the lag head, which gains VH bit 15 at lags 1 and 2 (2 columns).
